      "unit": "One complete scenario/seed run. Run every policy on identical trace events and cost configuration.",
      "paired_effect": "fixed group_int4 baseline metric minus candidate metric; positive denotes candidate improvement for latency, work, and bytes",
      "ablation": "adaptive is the legacy aggregate-size policy. adaptive_exact uses the same exact per-page sizing and victim planning as adaptive_eviction but charges zero eviction penalty. Compare adaptive_eviction with adaptive_exact to isolate the charged externality; do not attribute all differences from legacy adaptive to eviction pricing.",
      "primary_aggregation": "For each scenario, compute p95 among resumed sessions within each run, then summarize paired per-run p95 differences over evaluation seeds. Do not pool all requests into one percentile.",
